  "answer": "## What change is needed for `@mui` imports in `variant-prop` codemod?\n\nThe `variant-prop` codemod lives in **`packages/mui-codemod/src/v5.0.0/variant-prop.js`** and is responsible for:\n1. Finding JSX components (notably `TextField`, `Select`, `FormControl`)\n2. Ensuring they receive the correct `variant` prop value (e.g. `\"standard\"`, `\"outlined\"`, etc.)\n3. Updating imports to match the v5 module layout\n\nFrom the provided excerpts, the codemod currently rewrites based on imports matching the **Material UI v4 paths** such as:\n- `@material-ui/core/TextField`\n- `@material-ui/core/Select`\n- `@material-ui/core/FormControl`\n\nThat logic is exercised by the test fixtures:\n- **`packages/mui-codemod/src/v5.0.0/variant-prop.test/mui-import.actual.js`** (input) uses `@material-ui/core/...` imports (v4-style)\n- **`packages/mui-codemod/src/v5.0.0/variant-prop.test/mui-import.expected.js`** (output) verifies the codemod’s intended result (and—per the PR description you included—“Fixed by adding `@mui/material` match.”)\n\n## Where `@mui` support should be added\n\nTo support `@mui` imports, the codemod’s import-matching logic in **`packages/mui-codemod/src/v5.0.0/variant-prop.js`** needs to treat both import base patterns as valid targets:\n\n- `@material-ui/core/*`  (existing)\n- `@mui/material/*` (missing, needs to be added)\n\nConcretely, the “for each specifier” / “filter value match material core … affected import declaration …” portion of **`variant-prop.js`** should extend its matcher so that when the local specifiers come from `@mui/material/...`, it still inserts the `variant` prop in the same way and rewrites/normalizes imports accordingly.\n\n## Evidence in tests\n\nThe fixtures show only `@material-ui/core/...` being handled in the excerpted “expected/actual” snapshots:\n- `mui-import.actual.js` and `mui-import.expected.js` both include `@material-ui/core/...` (v4)\n- The PR note says the fix was “adding `@mui/material` match”, implying the updated codemod now recognizes `@mui/material/...` sources even if the excerpted snippets don’t show the `@mui` case directly.\n\nIf you want, I can help you locate the exact matcher in `variant-prop.js` once you provide the full source body (the current excerpt is too summarized to cite the precise lines).",
